## Overview

The scraper (`lament-scrapper`) is a Node.js CLI tool that automates music ingestion. It orchestrates multiple external services to build the Lament music library.

## Pipeline

```
Input (CSV / Spotify URL / Search query)
        │
        ▼
1. Spotify API ──► Fetch metadata (track, album, artist)
        │
        ▼
2. YouTube Search ──► Find matching audio
        │
        ▼
3. yt-dlp ──► Download audio
        │
        ▼
4. FFmpeg ──► Convert to HLS (m3u8 + ts segments)
        │
        ▼
5. Sharp ──► Process cover art (resize, WebP)
        │
        ▼
6. Genius ──► Fetch lyrics
        │
        ▼
7. R2 Upload ──► Store audio + images
        │
        ▼
8. LibSQL ──► Insert metadata
```

## Entry Points

The main entry point is `src/index.ts`. The scraper can be run in different modes:

```bash
# Full scrape from CSV input
bun run dev

# Individual scripts
bun run backup        # Backup database
bun run restore       # Restore from backup
bun run reconcile     # Reconcile DB with R2
bun run repair        # Repair metadata
```

## Anti-Duplication

Tracks have an `original_id` field (Spotify ID or YouTube ID) marked as `UNIQUE` to prevent duplicate entries.
